lah and San Isabel.\n\nThis includes the following high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.","ends":"2026-08-23T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f7765e9af6e59655c34c85e8d4c9b44db6c8e9f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f7765e9af6e59655c34c85e8d4c9b44db6c8e9f.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 23 at 3:25PM MDT until August 23 at 6:30PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"FFWPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Northern Aspen Acres Burn Scar in...\nEastern Custer County in southeastern Colorado...\nWest Central Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 630 PM MDT.\n\n* At 325 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Northern Aspen Acres Burn Scar. Flash flooding\nis ongoing or expected to begin shortly. Excessive rainfall over\nthe burn scar will result in debris flow moving through the Red\nCreek, Peck Creek and Rock Creek Drainages. The debris flow can\nconsist of rock, mud, vegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Northern Aspen Acres Burn\nScar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nNorthern Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Eastern Custer and West Central Pueblo\nCounties.","ends":"2026-08-23T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8a8374d917c15b42e6fa9c48fd50770ccd9db89a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8a8374d917c15b42e6fa9c48fd50770ccd9db89a.001.1"},{"event":"Severe 